# Authors: Simon Davidson & Claude | Created 2026-08-20 | Last modified 2026-08-20
#
# Wide (three-word) TASK decode, WIDE_NTGT=1 / TGT_COUNT_SZ=7.
#
# The narrow TASK caps usage counts at 15; Monarch at nblocks=40 needs 85. The
# wide form is selected per instruction by TASK word 1 bit 31 (previously
# reserved and always zero), so it ADDS a form rather than changing one.
#
# Proves: narrow and wide encodings of the SAME task decode to a byte-identical
# scheduler entry (both forms in one instruction stream); counts of 16..127
# survive; and a wide TASK consumes exactly three program words without its
# word 2 / word 3 being decoded as instructions.
#
# -define WDBG adds a per-cycle fetch-FSM trace.
xrun -sv -timescale 1ns/1ps -access wrc -top tb_sch_wide \
  sch_entry.v sch_table.v buffer_state_entry.v acc_hw_buffer_tracker.v \
  sch_buffer_state.v prog_cache.v scheduler.v tb_sch_wide.v
